re-mach
=======

re-mach is a new kernel, written from scratch in Rust. It is free
software under the GNU General Public License, version 2 or, at your
option, any later version (LICENSES/GPL-2.0-or-later.txt).

It is inspired by GNU Mach, the microkernel of the GNU Hurd, at commit
fa3026b9d18261dce7152b93c4b106798404bae3 of
<https://git.savannah.gnu.org/git/hurd/gnumach.git>. re-mach
reproduces GNU Mach's interface to user space, and much of its code
was written by reading GNU Mach's: its algorithms, its data structures
and its behaviour.

re-mach is a fully new implementation, but it was not made in a clean
room. Its files were written with GNU Mach's sources open, and a file
of re-mach may draw on several files of GNU Mach. The work as a whole
is therefore treated as derived from GNU Mach, and the respect owed to
GNU Mach's authors is kept here, in this single file, rather than in
each source file. A source file that draws on an upstream says so in
one line,

    // Inspired by GNU Mach; see COPYRIGHT.

and carries the copyright of its own authors only.


